     "id": "v2-proposal-j10-211127-root",
     "type": "question",
     "label": null,
     "prompt": "The point $(-12,5)$ is $13$ units from the origin and lies on the terminal ray of the angle $\\theta$. Write down the values of $\\sin\\theta$, $\\cos\\theta$ and $\\tan\\theta$.",
     "answer": {
      "short": "$\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{5}{13},\\ \\cos\\theta=-\\dfrac{12}{13},\\ \\tan\\theta=-\\dfrac{5}{12}$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x&=-12,\\ y=5,\\ r=13\\\\\\sin\\theta&=\\frac{y}{r}=\\frac{5}{13}\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{x}{r}=-\\frac{12}{13}\\\\\\tan\\theta&=\\frac{y}{x}=-\\frac{5}{12}\\end{align*}$$"
     },
